{"id": 4613568008, "verdict": "NOT_RELEVANT", "reasoning": "This is a borderline call. Several criteria pass, but the level criterion fails.

PASSES: (1) Role type: 'Research Engineer' is in Ananya's target_roles. The representative projects are mostly engineering work: RL training infrastructure, distributed experiment management on GPU clusters, training environments and evaluations, profiling and optimization, caching, debugging distributed systems, testing frameworks and APIs. Publishing is explicitly not required ('need not have academic research experience or publication history'). The role does still describe 'fundamental research in reinforcement learning' and contributing to research direction. (2) Skills: the required section names 2+ technologies (Python, Trio, PyTorch/TensorFlow/JAX), and Ananya has shipped at least 2 of them (Python, PyTorch), so the skills test passes. Kubernetes, which she has not shipped, appears only under 'Strong candidates may have', so it is not a core requirement. Trio and async/concurrent programming are a gap but not disqualifying alone. (3) Location: San Francisco, CA and New York City, NY are US-based, and she is willing to relocate within the US. (4) Sponsorship: the posting says 'We do sponsor visas!', which satisfies her needs_sponsorship=true.

FAILS: (5) Level is not realistic for a new grad finishing an MS in December 2026. The posting lists 'Have industry experience in machine learning research' as a baseline qualification. Ananya's only industry experience is an 8-month ML Engineer co-op building an applied RAG prototype and a fine-tuned classifier, which is applied ML engineering rather than ML research. The stated salary band of $500,000–$850,000 is far above new-grad pay and signals a senior-level role, and the posting says years of experience 'correlate with the internal job level.' The core work, architecting RL infrastructure across GPU clusters and debugging distributed systems at frontier-model scale, also points to experienced hires. No explicit '3+ years' or PhD requirement is stated, which is why this is borderline. Taken together, though, the industry-research-experience requirement and the senior compensation band make this an unrealistic target for her current level. Verdict: NOT_RELEVANT.", "resume_fields_cited": ["education", "experience", "target_roles", "skills.languages", "skills.ml_nlp", "skills.familiar_with_not_shipped", "needs_sponsorship", "willing_to_relocate_us", "personal.location"], "posting_fields_cited": ["title", "content", "location.name"]}
